WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.730
This story is one that lightly describes the ordinary daily lives of the three Minami sisters.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.340
Please don't expect too much from it.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.300
Also, watch in a bright room,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.960
and stay 3 meters away from the TV while watching.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:22.370
Kana

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:22.710
Chiaki

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.500
Haruka

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.040
Strange School

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.140
I've decided. I'm going to quit school.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.010
Oh, is that right?

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:10.760
Maki, we only got to know you for a short time, but it's been fun.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:11.640
Eh?

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.540
Ah! Atsuko, your fried egg looks nice.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.680
Trade one with me.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.720
Eh? It doesn't match up to your cooking, Haruka.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:20.810
That's not right, is it?

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.610
That's not how it's supposed to go, is it?

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.910
Stop me!

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.080
You two!

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:28.500
You want us to stop you?

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:29.720
Yeah.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.290
Ask her the reason

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:37.010
So then, why do you want to quit school?

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.930
T-The reason...

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.990
That's, um...

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.880
Do I... have to say it?

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.890
You don't have to make it feel that serious.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.750
You've been saying for three straight days that you want to quit school.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.050
It's about time we start ignoring it.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:59.780
T-Thank you for your gentle scolding.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.820
So what part of school are you unhappy about?

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.830
The uniform. I have issues with the uniform.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:07.860
The uniform?

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.990
Is the uniform not cute enough or something?

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:12.120
That's not it!

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.700
Something more fundamental!

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.370
To me...

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.270
It's this!

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:31.940
We're being forced to wear skirts!

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.890
This is sexual harassment on a national level!

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.660
It's troublesome when our panties can be seen in some situations, right?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.660
Furthermore, sometimes we can't even tell if they're visible or not.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.020
Well, they're not visible all that often...

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.070
But that's only because you don't notice!

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:53.440
Um...

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.830
then you should wear bloomers on top of your underwear...

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.400
Eh? Where did my bread go?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.420
Didn't you eat it?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.580
U-Um...

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.470
I wonder what happened...

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:05.790
You ate it already.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.770
Minami said earlier...

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.840
that underwear is rarely seen!

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:19.180
When I dove under the table to look for my bread, I saw it!

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.390
The thing which Minami said is rarely seen...

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.390
Those...

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.540
Minami's...

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.310
White pan-

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:29.520
Certainly, bread is white on the inside.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.500
White bread.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:47.380
Yes. I saw that white bread.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:48.990
Bread?

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.430
Of course.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.720
U-Um...

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.410
Anyway, in your usual daily life, it rarely gets seen, right?

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:57.030
Um...

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.180
Even though I saw it just by picking up bread?

00:04:59.180 --> 00:04:59.970
Like I said, going under the desk is-

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:01.210
Um...
Like I said, going under the desk is-

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.890
Like I said, going under the desk is-

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:07.660
Shouldn't you just wear bloomers or something under the skirt?!

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.260
That's right!

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.480
You should've said that earlier.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.910
Y-Yes.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:29.010
Haruka!

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.850
She's wearing it!

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.280
Lift her skirt up for a bit!

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.300
Eh?

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.920
Hurry, hurry!

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.420
Isn't that great?

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.630
It's perfect!

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.110
Try it yourself.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:44.900
Minami-ke!

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.270
In other news...

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.520
After the loincloth festival ended successfully,

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.290
this year's Loincloth King has suddenly relinquished his throne,

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.570
so the festivities are starting up once again.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:58.040
We have Aota reporting live from the location.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.870
You were late today, Haruka.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:00.220
Aota-san?
You were late today, Haruka.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:01.070
Yes, I was busy with the committee.
Aota-san?

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.030
Yes, I was busy with the committee.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.110
Aota-san?
Yes, I was busy with the committee.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:03.970
Were you alone?

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:04.890
Uh, we're having some technical difficulties.
Were you alone?

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.740
There was another guy from my class with me.
Uh, we're having some technical difficulties.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:07.690
Sorry about that.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:08.720
A guy...
Sorry about that.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.390
You two weren't doing anything strange, right?

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.940
Hey, Kana!

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.440
Don't say strange things in front of Chiaki!

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:23.710
What?

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.770
What part of "strange things" is so strange?

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:29.100
What are those strange things?

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.560
Kana, you can't.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.570
Don't teach Chiaki strange things.

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:40.530
Strange things as in strange things you can't teach?

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:41.870
It's not that!

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.720
Anyway...

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:47.140
Listen, Chiaki!

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.790
When a man and woman are together,

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:51.890
that's when they'll do strange things.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:52.850
K-Kana!

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:56.000
Like I said, what are those strange things?

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.480
That's... um...

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.090
You know...

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:04.940
Surely something unrivaled... something fun...

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.570
Hey.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.980
I-It's okay!

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:10.260
I censored my words with mosaics.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.540
That's right. This talk is over.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.610
Chiaki, eat your vegetables.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:20.310
How is that fun?

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.780
Like I said, that's...

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.280
That's...

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.700
You know...

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.000
How is it, Haruka?

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.010
Eh?

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:34.850
In other news.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:38.130
To leave the "Number One Loincloth in Japan" record behind,

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:42.690
residents have started a new event of not changing their loincloths for several days.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.230
Bye bye!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.650
Be careful on your way home!

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:49.350
Chiaki!

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.390
Let's go home together.

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:52.680
Sure.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.880
Minami, Yoshino!

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.470
Want to stop by my house?

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.430
What are you going to do?

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.800
Well, just play games and stuff.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:06.140
Honestly, we were hoping you could help out with homework.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.280
That's a great idea.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.600
Minami, you're coming, right?

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:10.580
Let's go!

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.410
Could it be that...

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:14.750
we're going to do strange things?

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:15.960
Eh?

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.740
W-What are you saying so suddenly?!

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:20.930
Are you doubting me?!

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.010
Don't surprise me!

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:23.710
What, you aren't going to do it?

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.440
D-Don't want to do it, you say?!

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:30.090
Did you have something planned?

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.940
No, nothing.

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.110
You mean you're not interested in games?

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.370
No, I am.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.270
I'm really good.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.170
There's some cake left over from my older sister's birthday yesterday.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:42.860
You're not interested in cake?

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:44.540
No, I am.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.510
But more like, I want to hear more details on which store it's from and what kind of cake it is.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.730
Then let's go!

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:52.580
We can do homework on the side!

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.290
Are we going to do strange things on the side?

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:58.000
I didn't say that!

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.250
If it's a nice person and a good opportunity,

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.760
we don't have to do it on the side, it'll be the main thing.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.290
What are you making me say?!

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.940
What, am I not good enough?

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:10.440
Anyway, I'm not going to do anything.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.440
Well, it's okay.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.650
Let's go.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:16.800
Don't surprise me.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:19.660
Doubting me in a strange way all of a sudden...

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.830
About that...

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:24.080
Are those two going to do strange things?

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.000
Eh?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.950
Hey!

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:31.950
While the event of not changing loincloths has progressed the past few days,

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:36.970
a protest group has emerged today claiming that it's bad hygiene.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.210
Chiaki.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.670
Did you finish your homework at your friend's place?

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:48.850
Yes, but nothing strange happened.

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:53.740
Y-You're only an elementary school student...

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:55.640
Even I haven't done it yet!

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:58.810
That's right! It's too early! Even I haven't...

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:04.540
In our next story, the upcoming space age:

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.510
topics on loincloth development.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:19.470
So then,

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:24.850
Typhoon 14 and Local Heavy Rain were fighting in the office.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:25.810
Really?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.360
I wanted to see that...

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:30.420
And then? What happened?

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:33.110
Typhoon 14 kicked first,

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:37.190
but Local Heavy Rain was slightly ahead.

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.740
And then, the Unopened Plastic Umbrella entered...

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.210
W-Wait a minute.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:46.570
You were talking about a typhoon and heavy rain for a while...

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:47.500
What are you talking about?

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.100
Hey, is she serious?

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.120
It doesn't seem like she's joking.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.340
I-Is something wrong?

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.890
They're nicknames.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.380
Tanaka-sensei and Kawauchi-sensei.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:05.130
Unopened Plastic Umbrella is Katou-sensei.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:06.890
You made up those names.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.320
Huh? Is that right?

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.880
That's right!

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.100
So, they were fighting and everything...

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.940
but the real offender was actually Black Belly White Bear...

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.820
<i>Black Belly White Bear...</i>

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:31.870
In the end, the Lidless Teapot muddied the tea...

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.770
<i>Lidless Teapot...</i>

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:41.300
Nishioka Store

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.650
Nonetheless, Minami...

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:48.770
Y-Yeah?

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.280
The nicknames you made up are strokes of genius.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:54.050
Chiaki is a genius.

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:56.270
I don't remember them at all.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:12:00.580
Eh? But I thought you gave nicknames for every teacher!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:04.410
Chiaki isn't interested in things she's already completed.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.530
What are you talking about?

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:09.760
Well then, you should give nicknames to everyone else in class.

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:10.550
Eh?

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:13.750
W-We probably shouldn't do that.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:17.770
Chiaki will scoop out the vital parts mercilessly.

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.590
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:23.340
Then, you should get a nickname first.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:24.800
All right!

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.220
Come!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.390
Mako-chan.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:31.860
That's so normal!

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:34.770
Or rather, it's so cute it's embarrassing!

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.180
Don't you have anything else?!

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:38.230
There is, right?!

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.400
Idiotic Child.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.030
That's straight!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.740
It's exactly that.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:45.330
It's more like impressions than nicknames.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.530
Which one is better?

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:48.160
Eh?

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:54.660
Then, Mako-chan...

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.500
Shuuichi is next.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:12:59.420
Eh?

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.840
Naming

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:11.250
Those nicknames are made from your name, your body, or some habit...

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:14.210
from the person's peculiar traits, right?

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:18.110
If Shuuichi doesn't have any part that stands out, wouldn't that be difficult?

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:25.990
Plain Yogurt.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.420
It's decided!

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.990
Shall we mix in some sugar?!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.230
Stop that, Mako-chan.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.500
Okay, next!

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:41.800
My nickname... is Student A.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.210
I'm Student B.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:45.710
Um...
Plain Yogurt

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:48.200
Did we give names to everyone?
Plain Yogurt

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:50.280
Only Minami herself is left.
Plain Yogurt

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:51.180
Plain Yogurt

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.060
Eh?

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.150
Make a nickname for myself?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.410
Who else is going to do it?!

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:11.450
Princess.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.830
Princess?!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.790
What's wrong, Minami?!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.500
Are you losing your touch for making nicknames?!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.750
No, you know...

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.380
isn't it cruel to make a nickname for yourself?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.500
Still, aside from that...!

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.300
Shut up, fool.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:29.220
I'm no fool, I'm the Idiotic Child!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.680
I accepted my own nickname!

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:37.890
Minami-ke!

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:48.780
Now, everyone!

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.280
It's time to clean up!

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.910
Makoto, we're almost done.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.620
Shuuichi, what's my position?

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.120
Well, I guess you can pick up the dust.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.960
All right! I'll pick up all the dust!

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.710
Shut up and do it, fool.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.630
Hey, Minami!

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:10.550
Is that the right attitude to have when you ask people to do things?

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:13.470
When you ask people to pick up the dust,

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.140
it's natural to say "please pick up the dust," right?!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:23.730
Stop talking, please get down and pick up the dust already.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:24.730
You fool.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.740
"Please get down" is too polite.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:29.780
On the contrary...

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.700
There's another part that should bother you more.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:35.620
All right.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.330
Now, come!

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.460
Don't come toward me!

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.920
You back off too much.

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.340
You didn't pick up the dust at all.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.590
You don't have any talent at picking up dust.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:53.220
Even with that big mouth.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.800
W-Wait a minute!

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:59.430
It might be true that I made a mistake.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:00.230
However!

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:02.730
Am I the only one responsible?!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.440
No, certainly not!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:07.900
We're not cleaning by ourselves!

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.400
We're working as a team!

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.110
Are you saying it's my fault for handling the broom?

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:17.080
No, I'm just saying the importance of fighting as a team...

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:19.540
You, step down from picking up dust.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.370
Stepping Down

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.120
Transferring the Duties

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:28.090
You said earlier that cleanup is done as a team.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:28.800
Right!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:31.380
It's exactly that.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.130
Even if it's just cleaning,

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:36.930
if you let your guard down, think of what disaster would befall the team.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.680
You understand, right?

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:39.760
Yes!

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:40.680
I do!

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:46.150
Chiaki?

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.780
Are you okay, Chiaki?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.990
You, go bring some buckets of water.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.160
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.870
I came with water!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.450
Go stand.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.330
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.790
Well then, let's gather up the dust again.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.130
Right.

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:20.060
Now we just have to throw the trash out.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.430
I'll go.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.310
No, me!

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:24.230
Stand.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.350
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:49.000
What are you doing this late at night?

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.090
No, I was told to stand!

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.960
Minami-ke!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.060
Hey, Chiaki.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.610
What are you doing?

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:11.400
Yes?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:14.030
I'm studying.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.490
Don't study in the living room!

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:20.570
When you study here, it makes me feel like an idiot!

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:29.170
Don't ignore me!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:33.380
I want to go to a good junior high school, so don't get in my way.

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:36.510
What, are you making fun of my school?

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.970
Even though Haruka went to the same school?

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:46.270
T-That's because... she picked a nearby school for our sake, right?

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.180
It was like that for senior high school as well.

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:52.150
Only you get to go to a good school...

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.150
D-Damn you!

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.650
Let's see, let's see.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:58.780
How good a student are you?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.910
Let's ask some questions.

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:07.660
In May of one year, there were four Tuesdays and Fridays.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.500
What day was May 5th of that year?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:11.420
Wednesday.

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:16.090
I-It's Wednesday!

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:17.090
Right.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.090
It's Wednesday...

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.300
But...

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:25.060
This question... which page is it on in this book?

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.060
Huh?

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:27.970
How should I know?!

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.730
Knowing this is not useful at all.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.020
Oh, maybe it's that.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:38.530
Maybe you're studying in the living room so Haruka can praise you?

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.400
D-Damn you!

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:45.740
Well, you might be a good student...

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:47.660
but only an elementary school student.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:54.830
Then, to show how much the current junior high school student is worth,

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:57.340
let's ask some questions.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:00.760
A star that's a star, but this star tastes sour... what is it?

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.680
Answer:
Dried Plum

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.220
A failure.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:07.810
It's true that it's not sweet...

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:13.060
When it wears a red hat, it sheds a tear and becomes smaller.

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:14.690
What is it?

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:16.040
Candle

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.820
Answer:
Candle

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:17.860
Fans of the Toyo Carps during consecutive defeats.
Answer:
Candle

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.320
Fans of the Toyo Carps during consecutive defeats.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:21.610
My bad.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.820
They'll definitely win it next year.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.830
Something that can be seen while sitting down, but can't be seen while standing up.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.290
What is it?

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:35.040
Give a serious answer once in a while.

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:44.800
W-What?

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:46.550
Where are you looking?

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:47.930
Panties!

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:50.010
The soles of your feet! Fool!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:54.100
Whenever a man and woman are together,

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.940
explain the strange things that happen in 400 words.

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:00.940
That would be... that would be...

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:07.620
"That would be, that would be strange things, you know."

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:10.030
I can't understand it with something like this!

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:13.660
Go to a good school and have them teach you.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:15.580
I'm home!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.250
Ah, you two are studying?

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:23.170
Please explain to us what strange things mean!

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:25.010
Eh?

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.140
I-In writing?

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:33.520
Um...

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:37.020
That's... That's...

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:39.610
Well well, putting that aside, let's hear your opinions regarding dinner.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:39.650
"Well well, putting that aside..."
Well well, putting that aside, let's hear your opinions regarding dinner.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:41.980
"Well well, putting that aside..."

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:45.200
"Let's hear your opinions regarding dinner."

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:50.910
Udon!

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.080
Curry!

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:54.830
Okay! Let's do curry udon!

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.540
Okay!

